/*
===============================================================================
Script 1 of 3: Create Database and Schemas
===============================================================================
Script Purpose:
    This script creates a new database named 'DataWarehouse' after checking if it
    already exists. If the database exists, it is dropped and recreated.
    Additionally, the script sets up three schemas within the database:
    'bronze', 'silver', and 'gold'.

WARNING:
    Running this script will drop the entire 'DataWarehouse' database if it exists.
    All data in the database will be permanently deleted. Proceed with caution
    and ensure you have proper backups before running this script.

===============================================================================
SETUP GUIDE - READ THIS BEFORE RUNNING
===============================================================================

Where this script fits (run the scripts in this order):
    1) 01_init_database.sql    <- THIS SCRIPT (database + schemas)
    2) 02_ddl_bronze.sql       (creates the 6 empty bronze tables)
    3) load_bronze.sql         (creates the procedure that loads the CSV files)
       then:  EXEC bronze.load_bronze;

Requirements:
    - Microsoft SQL Server (any edition, e.g. Express/Developer) and a client
      such as SQL Server Management Studio (SSMS) or Azure Data Studio.
    - A login that is allowed to create/drop databases (e.g. sysadmin or dbcreator).
    - No source files are needed for this script. The CSV files are only used
      later by load_bronze.sql.

What the script does, step by step:
    1) USE master
           Switches to the 'master' system database. You cannot drop a database
           while you are connected inside it, so we work from master.
    2) Drop the old database if it exists
           SINGLE_USER WITH ROLLBACK IMMEDIATE disconnects everyone else and
           cancels their open transactions so the DROP does not get blocked.
    3) CREATE DATABASE DataWarehouse
           Creates a fresh, empty database with default settings.
    4) CREATE SCHEMA bronze / silver / gold
           Schemas are folders inside the database that organise the tables
           by data quality layer (Medallion Architecture):

           bronze  Raw data, loaded as-is from the source files (CSV).
                   No cleaning, no transformations.
           silver  Cleaned and standardised data (fixed types, removed
                   duplicates, handled nulls, etc.).
                   Not used by these scripts yet - the schema is just prepared.
           gold    Business-ready data (e.g. fact and dimension views for
                   reporting and analytics).
                   Not used by these scripts yet - the schema is just prepared.

Naming:
    - The database name 'DataWarehouse' is a choice, not a requirement. If you
      want a different name, replace 'DataWarehouse' everywhere in this script
      (the IF EXISTS check, ALTER DATABASE, DROP DATABASE, CREATE DATABASE
      and USE). Then make sure that database is selected before running the
      other two scripts.
    - Schema names (bronze, silver, gold) are used by the other scripts, so keep
      them unchanged unless you update those scripts too.

How to verify it worked:
    SELECT name FROM sys.databases WHERE name = 'DataWarehouse';
    SELECT name FROM DataWarehouse.sys.schemas
    WHERE name IN ('bronze', 'silver', 'gold');
    (You should get 1 row for the first query and 3 rows for the second.)

Common errors and fixes:
    "CREATE DATABASE permission denied in database 'master'"
        -> Connect with a login that has permission to create databases.
    "Database 'DataWarehouse' is in use" / cannot drop
        -> Another session is connected. The script already forces
           SINGLE_USER, but make sure your own query window is not
           sitting inside DataWarehouse when you run it (stay on master).
    "There is already an object named 'bronze' in the database"
        -> Happens if you run only the schema part twice. Run the whole
           script from the top so the database is dropped and recreated.
===============================================================================
*/

USE master;
GO

-- Drop and recreate the 'DataWarehouse' database
IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.databases WHERE name = 'DataWarehouse')
BEGIN
    ALTER DATABASE DataWarehouse SET SINGLE_USER WITH ROLLBACK IMMEDIATE;
    DROP DATABASE DataWarehouse;
END;
GO

-- Create the 'DataWarehouse' database
CREATE DATABASE DataWarehouse;
GO

USE DataWarehouse;
GO

-- Create Schemas
CREATE SCHEMA bronze;
GO

CREATE SCHEMA silver;
GO

CREATE SCHEMA gold;
GO
